            <div xml:id="d149">

                <pb facs="0237" n="215" sameAs="frus:frus1951v02/pg215"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">399.10–UPU/1–2451:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                            Embassy in Brazil
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">priority</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">niact</hi>
                        
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1951-01-24T15:00:00-05:00">January 24, 1951—3
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>507. Ref Depcirtel 384 Jan 15 and urtel 929 Jan 18.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d149-f1"/>
                    USRep
                    UPU Conference Cairo informs Dept vote on US proposal re Chi representation as
                    well as Sov motion seat Chi Commie will be taken at morning session Jan 25. No
                    Del has been willing second US proposal, although Arg Rep will speak in favor.
                    Braz Rep has indicated USDel he instructed
                    vote for US proposal but not speak on subj and construes this mean he cannot
                    second US motion. Since situation precarious, request you in your discretion ask
                        FonOff urgently instruct Braz Rep second
                    and speak in favor US motion.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
